        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_75f9af0d95fb46b0ab93522bd3c23695",
      "statement": "The per-cell input gate governs blockConcurrencyWhile: while held no new event is delivered, nesting is counted, acquire cannot fail because delivery points check is_open first, refused events simply stay on the shell's job channel (the core models no queue), and abandon() covers the one exit path that runs no JS.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/gate.rs#L101-L144",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a7f4eb074c88a1fd1d1ddd59abb11a4f8dae21790645bb182b6e19d114254deb:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/gate.rs#L3-L56",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5e1691e8c49f8231867b8a0418436930d76ade26087f64e8b25bb74ba7d90382:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_92c14d278c0b43209f9801b96f284318",
      "statement": "The output gate is one choke point: Channel enumerates every state-revealing route, State::output applies one durability rule without matching on the channel, and earlier split mechanisms (core reader gate, shell WebSocket queue, in-handler check) were replaced because each had a different view of outstanding writes.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/output_gate.rs#L29-L40",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:51a99194a67fb7e92c15ed80326ebb2706745cd55237807505a951c9522368b9:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/output_gate.rs#L5-L17",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d163df94690fe2d831bf4c668bf9110800caaa25fd8d9bdac6cd139a725368ff:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c874e9056cfd474fabc98dc97704eadf",
      "statement": "Alarm firing opens its own barrier in the same per-cell map (GateOwner::Alarm) when a consuming commit is unproven, so read-only outputs trail an alarm's unproven write exactly as they trail a request's.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/output_gate.rs#L42-L57",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:03561f1334a65c9e3d09b994dd4f384a01bb7106383d403ec9c61557310cea9c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_35b19ee4c1e24c99813feeae7e49f19a",
      "statement": "Peer-forward retry is bounded by how far the attempt got: NotOwner and NeverConnected failures get one retry each, Ambiguous failures never retry, protecting at-most-once cell execution.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/routing.rs#L3-L18",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2c63c963ca0d70dcd700d3910a0400e01490ad5d4d5f0b7661633b902165460e:"
        },
        {
