        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4b295a3796f74367a89166a272fdf728",
      "statement": "Restore-source choice is a pure durability predicate: a previous-epoch local eviction snapshot may be reused only when the cell was not taken over and epoch > 1, because after takeover the other node's newer durable state is authoritative; local crash-epoch restore helpers were deleted with the external litestream backend.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/restore.rs#L3-L29",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:478ce647730881145ba9834a3caeb2d80f28f58f4ea691e460c1e748d5eef62f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_97a1691444304ac39efe220c55488397",
      "statement": "The isolate pool policy separates turns (in-flight CPU demand, released across awaits) from requests (heap affiliation pinning later turns to the same isolate), balancing placement on turns while admission and shedding act on requests.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/isolate.rs#L3-L27",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8b0c294de01bbf16e860632649e4e2d66243f1e012132bfd8cf8dc2a0aa27890:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b2006051798b4ce1b8b519ae26b9cdcc",
      "statement": "Network-input validation fences are pure predicates in the core: peer identity charset and two-sided clock window with replay retention >= the window; cell-scope charset excluding path separators plus the . and .. names with a 255-byte fleet-wide bound; and URL-authority shape checks so a hostile Host cannot make every Worker request throw in new URL().",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/cell.rs#L3-L46",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c65a796444a957ca97b1e4fc3fa80dc6bb930a53d50c23aad2944287f921fb8a:"
        },
        {
