    {
      "id": "claim_ddabd586c3814782b9a1bb88150cac90",
      "statement": "Reserved-class service policy is split by caller: the KV core keeps only addresses and bounds because request validation runs in JS, while the Queue core owns bounds, lease generation, retry, settlement fencing, and config validation, with the lease generation traveling in PlannedLease so a caller cannot forget to advance it.",
